#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Controls"
msgstr "Knobs an' Levers"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"One client runs on a desktop, a phone and a headset, so every action has a "
"way in from each of them. The keyboard has the most; touch, a gamepad and "
"the XR controllers carry the actions a match needs, and the Settings menu "
"reaches the rest -- including from a headset, where there is no keyboard at "
"all. This page is also the in-game help's (`/` or `?`)."
msgstr ""
"One client runs on a desktop, a phone an' a headset, so ever' action's got a "
"way in from each of 'em. The keyboard's got the most; touch, a gamepad an' "
"the XR controllers carry what a match needs, an' the Settings menu reaches "
"the rest -- even from a headset, where there ain't no keyboard at all. This "
"here page is also the in-game help's (`/` or `?`)."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Keyboard"
msgstr "Keyboard"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Driving"
msgstr "Drivin'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`W` / `S` or `Up` / `Down` — move forward/backward"
msgstr "`W` / `S` or `Up` / `Down` — go forward/back up"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`A` / `D` or `Left` / `Right` — turn left/right"
msgstr "`A` / `D` or `Left` / `Right` — turn left/right"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Enter` — shoot"
msgstr "`Enter` — shoot"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Tab` — jump"
msgstr "`Tab` — jump"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Space` — drop flag"
msgstr "`Space` — drop the flag"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`I` or right-click — identify the tank in your sights, and lock a Guided "
"Missile onto it"
msgstr ""
"`I` or right-click — figger out who's in yer sights, an' lock a Guided "
"Missile on 'em"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Delete` — self-destruct, after a five second countdown; `Delete` again "
"calls it off"
msgstr ""
"`Delete` — blow yerself up after a five second countdown; `Delete` again "
"calls it off"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`9` or `/autopilot [roger|ace]` — autopilot: the pilot drives, aims and "
"shoots until pressed again. `Settings -> Autopilot` chooses the pilot "
"without a keyboard. You can still drive while it does, to help it out of a "
"corner -- see [Combining inputs](#combining-inputs)"
msgstr ""
"`9` or `/autopilot [roger|ace]` — autopilot: the pilot drives, aims an' "
"shoots till ya press it again. `Settings -> Autopilot` picks the pilot "
"without no keyboard. Ya can still drive while it does, to help it outta a "
"corner -- see [Mixin' inputs](#combining-inputs)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`P` — pause/resume"
msgstr "`P` — take a breather/git back to it"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Chat"
msgstr "Jawin'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`N` — open chat (or click the `Send` button)"
msgstr "`N` — open chat (or click the `Send` button)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Enter` — send chat (while chat input is focused, or click `Send` again)"
msgstr "`Enter` — send chat (while yer typin' in chat, or click `Send` again)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`1` / `2` / `3` / `4` / `5` — switch chat tab (`All` / `Chat` / `Server` / "
"`Misc` / `Debug`)"
msgstr ""
"`1` / `2` / `3` / `4` / `5` — switch chat tab (`All` / `Chat` / `Server` / "
"`Misc` / `Debug`)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`[` / `]` — previous/next chat tab"
msgstr "`[` / `]` — last/next chat tab"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Tab` — while typing, complete a player, command or flag name; `@` starts a "
"mention and `#` a player's slot number"
msgstr ""
"`Tab` — while typin', finish off a player, command or flag name; `@` starts "
"a mention an' `#` a player's slot number"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Up` / `Down` — while typing, recall earlier lines; type the start of a line "
"first to recall only the ones beginning that way"
msgstr ""
"`Up` / `Down` — while typin', fetch back earlier lines; type how a line "
"starts first to fetch only the ones that start thataway"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`.` — reply to last direct-message sender"
msgstr "`.` — holler back at whoever last sent ya a direct message"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`,` — message nemesis target"
msgstr "`,` — message yer nemesis"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Page Up` / `Page Down` — scroll chat history"
msgstr "`Page Up` / `Page Down` — scroll back through the jawin'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`End` — jump chat to newest message"
msgstr "`End` — jump chat to the newest message"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Drag across the history while chat is open to select it, then copy; typing "
"carries on in the input"
msgstr ""
"Drag across the history while chat's open to pick it out, then copy; typin' "
"keeps on goin' in the input"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "View and panels"
msgstr "Lookin' an' panels"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Esc` — back out one step: exit chat input, leave fullscreen, leave mouse "
"steering, then open Settings. Pressing it again closes Settings, so it is "
"always safe to press one more time"
msgstr ""
"`Esc` — back out one step: quit chat input, leave fullscreen, leave mouse "
"steerin', then open Settings. Pressin' it again shuts Settings, so it's "
"always safe to mash it one more time"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`M` — toggle mouse steering"
msgstr "`M` — flip mouse steerin' on or off"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`C` — cycle camera mode"
msgstr "`C` — cycle camera mode"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`O` — toggle operator panel"
msgstr "`O` — flip the operator panel"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`F` — toggle fullscreen"
msgstr "`F` — flip fullscreen"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`` ` `` — toggle debug HUD"
msgstr "`` ` `` — flip the debug HUD"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`=` or `+` or `Numpad +` — zoom radar out (increase range)"
msgstr "`=` or `+` or `Numpad +` — zoom radar out (see further)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`-` or `Numpad -` — zoom radar in (decrease range)"
msgstr "`-` or `Numpad -` — zoom radar in (see closer)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`\\` — reset radar zoom to the default medium range (half the world's radar "
"limit, which is the world size unless the map says otherwise)"
msgstr ""
"`\\` — set radar zoom back to the regular medium range (half the world's "
"radar limit, which is the world size 'less the map says different)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Settings -> Radar: ...` — cycle Short/Medium/Long radar presets"
msgstr "`Settings -> Radar: ...` — cycle Short/Medium/Long radar settin's"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`B` — toggle the voice microphone"
msgstr "`B` — flip the voice microphone"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Settings -> Audio Settings` — set the game, voice, and microphone levels, "
"and choose the voice channel: All, Nearby, or Team"
msgstr ""
"`Settings -> Audio Settings` — set the game, voice, an' microphone levels, "
"an' pick the voice channel: All, Nearby, or Team"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`/` or `?` — show/hide help panel"
msgstr "`/` or `?` — show/hide the help panel"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`🎤` beside the gear — the microphone, as `B` is: a green border means you "
"are transmitting and a red one means you are not, and the hover text names "
"the channel it would speak on"
msgstr ""
"`🎤` next to the gear — the microphone, same as `B`: a green border means yer "
"on the air an' a red one means ya ain't, an' the hover text names the "
"channel it'd talk on"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`▲` beside the gear — hide the scoreboard and chat, leaving the name row and "
"the chat tabs; `▼` brings them back. Typing a message borrows the chat "
"window until you are done with it, and `U` or `7` borrows the scoreboard "
"until the hunt cursor closes; tapping a chat tab opens chat for good. Small "
"screens start collapsed"
msgstr ""
"`▲` next to the gear — hide the scoreboard an' chat, leavin' the name row "
"an' the chat tabs; `▼` brings 'em back. Typin' a message borrows the chat "
"window till yer done with it, an' `U` or `7` borrows the scoreboard till the "
"hunt cursor shuts; tappin' a chat tab opens chat fer good. Little screens "
"start out folded up"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Settings -> Anaglyph 3D` — red/cyan glasses; `Settings -> VR Mode` enters a "
"WebXR headset"
msgstr ""
"`Settings -> Anaglyph 3D` — red/cyan glasses; `Settings -> VR Mode` gits ya "
"into a WebXR headset"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Menus"
msgstr "Menus"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Up` / `Down` — previous/next control, including from inside a text field"
msgstr "`Up` / `Down` — last/next control, even from inside a text field"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Left` / `Right` — change the focused control: move a slider, pick the next "
"choice. In a text field they move the cursor instead"
msgstr ""
"`Left` / `Right` — change the control yer on: slide a slider, pick the next "
"choice. In a text field they move the cursor instead"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Tab` / `Shift+Tab` — previous/next control"
msgstr "`Tab` / `Shift+Tab` — last/next control"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Home` / `End` — first/last control"
msgstr "`Home` / `End` — first/last control"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`Enter` or `Space` — press the focused control"
msgstr "`Enter` or `Space` — press the control yer on"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Click or tap a row that walks a list: the title steps back and the current "
"option steps forward. The `‹` and `›` on the row mark the two halves"
msgstr ""
"Click or tap a row that walks a list: the title steps back an' the current "
"pick steps forward. The `‹` an' `›` on the row mark the two halves"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"The help panel is read rather than operated, so there the arrows scroll it "
"and only `Left` / `Right` move focus"
msgstr ""
"The help panel's fer readin', not operatin', so there the arrows scroll it "
"an' only `Left` / `Right` move focus"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Hunting"
msgstr "Huntin'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Marking a player puts a cyan `◎` on their scoreboard row, a cyan ring on "
"their radar blip, and a beacon in the sky over them in their own tank colour "
"-- so several marked at once are still told apart at a glance. While one of "
"them is in your sights the HUD says **SPOTTED:** and a ping sounds once a "
"second from where they are. In Rabbit Chase the rabbit is marked for you, "
"and its beacon is cyan like its ring: everyone is hunting it, so everyone's "
"mark over it says so."
msgstr ""
"Markin' a player puts a cyan `◎` on their scoreboard row, a cyan ring on "
"their radar blip, an' a beacon in the sky over 'em in their own tank colour "
"-- so a bunch marked at once can still be told apart quick as a wink. While "
"one of 'em's in yer sights the HUD says **SPOTTED:** an' a ping sounds once "
"a second from where they're at. In Rabbit Chase the rabbit's marked fer ya, "
"an' its beacon's cyan like its ring: ever'body's huntin' it, so ever'body's "
"mark over it says so."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`U` — hunt: open the scoreboard cursor, and press it again on a running hunt "
"to clear every mark"
msgstr ""
"`U` — hunt: open the scoreboard cursor, an' press it again on a hunt that's "
"goin' to clear ever' mark"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`7` — add hunt: the same cursor, but committing adds to what is marked "
"rather than replacing it, and committing on a row already marked takes it off"
msgstr ""
"`7` — add hunt: the same cursor, but committin' adds to what's marked 'stead "
"of replacin' it, an' committin' on a row that's already marked takes it off"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Settings -> Hunt` — the same thing without a keyboard, for a phone or a "
"headset. Left and right step through `Clear` and then the players in "
"alphabetical order; select marks or unmarks whoever is shown, or clears "
"every mark on `Clear`. On a touch screen or with a mouse, tap a chevron to "
"step and anywhere else on the row to select"
msgstr ""
"`Settings -> Hunt` — the same thing without no keyboard, fer a phone or a "
"headset. Left an' right step through `Clear` an' then the players in "
"alphabet order; select marks or unmarks whoever's showin', or clears ever' "
"mark on `Clear`. On a touch screen or with a mouse, tap a chevron to step "
"an' anywhere else on the row to select"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"With the cursor open, the board's heading reads `*SEL*` and a pulsing `○` "
"sits on the row it is on, filling in to `◎` when you commit. `Up` / `Down` "
"move it, `Enter` commits, and `U` or `7` backs out keeping whatever was "
"already marked. `I` and `Space` move the cursor too, so a surface without "
"arrow keys can reach it"
msgstr ""
"With the cursor open, the board's headin' reads `*SEL*` an' a pulsin' `○` "
"sets on the row it's on, fillin' in to `◎` when ya commit. `Up` / `Down` "
"move it, `Enter` commits, an' `U` or `7` backs out keepin' whatever was "
"already marked. `I` an' `Space` move the cursor too, so somethin' without no "
"arrow keys can git to it"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "As an observer"
msgstr "Just a-watchin'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"As an Observer you have no tank. Drive and turn fly the camera instead, "
"`Tab` climbs and `Space` descends, and holding `Shift` makes drive tilt the "
"view up and down and turn slide it sideways. The camera rests at the eye "
"height of a tank on the ground, and travel stays level however the view is "
"tilted. Pausing and self-destruct do nothing."
msgstr ""
"As an Observer ya got no tank. Drive an' turn fly the camera instead, `Tab` "
"climbs an' `Space` goes down, an' holdin' `Shift` makes drive tilt the view "
"up an' down an' turn slide it sideways. The camera sets at the eye height of "
"a tank on the ground, an' travel stays level however the view's tilted. "
"Pausin' an' blowin' yerself up don't do nothin'."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`Enter` or `C` — step through everything: in each view, the leader first, "
"then every player, then on to the next view. The views are Free, Track, "
"Follow, Driving with, and Flag where a map has team flags"
msgstr ""
"`Enter` or `C` — step through ever'thing: in each view, the leader first, "
"then ever' player, then on to the next view. The views are Free, Track, "
"Follow, Driving with, an' Flag where a map's got team flags"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`I` or right-click — in the Free view, watch the tank in your sights, or "
"show the obstacle there: what it is, an outline round it, and its block from "
"the map file with the `group` blocks that placed it"
msgstr ""
"`I` or right-click — in the Free view, watch the tank in yer sights, or show "
"the obstacle there: what it is, an outline 'round it, an' its block from the "
"map file with the `group` blocks that put it there"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Right-click or tap an obstacle anywhere on screen, in any view and the "
"Overview most of all, to show it the same way"
msgstr ""
"Right-click or tap an obstacle anywhere on screen, in any view an' the "
"Overview most of all, to show it the same way"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Pick nothing -- the sky, or empty ground in the Overview -- or press the "
"panel's **World** button for the whole world: what is in it, faces, "
"textures, the map file's warnings and its largest meshes, each of which "
"shows that mesh"
msgstr ""
"Pick nothin' -- the sky, or bare ground in the Overview -- or press the "
"panel's **World** button fer the whole shebang: what's in it, faces, "
"textures, the map file's warnin's an' its biggest meshes, each of which "
"shows that mesh"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Click a scoreboard row to watch that player; click the marked row again to "
"go back to following the leader"
msgstr ""
"Click a scoreboard row to watch that player; click the marked row again to "
"go back to tailin' the leader"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Mouse"
msgstr "Mouse"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"`M` turns mouse steering on and off, and nothing else does: the keys never "
"take it away behind your back."
msgstr ""
"`M` turns mouse steerin' on an' off, an' nothin' else does: the keys won't "
"never take it away behind yer back."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "The targeting box"
msgstr "The aimin' box"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"The two boxes in the middle of the screen are the steering, as in BZFlag. "
"Where the cursor sits relative to their centre is what the tank does:"
msgstr ""
"The two boxes in the middle of the screen are the steerin', same as BZFlag. "
"Where the cursor sets compared to their middle is what the tank does:"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Inside the inner box, nothing.** It is the dead zone: park the cursor "
"there to stop."
msgstr ""
"**Inside the inner box, nothin'.** It's the dead zone: park the cursor there "
"to stop."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Between the boxes, more the further out.** Up is forward and down is "
"reverse; left and right turn. Each grows evenly from nothing at the inner "
"box's edge to full at the outer box's."
msgstr ""
"**Between the boxes, more the further out.** Up's forward an' down's "
"reverse; left an' right turn. Each one grows even from nothin' at the inner "
"box's edge to full at the outer box's."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**At or past the outer box, full.** Each axis stops growing on its own, so "
"running the cursor out past the top keeps the tank at full speed and leaves "
"left and right free to steer."
msgstr ""
"**At or past the outer box, full.** Each way quits growin' on its own, so "
"runnin' the cursor out past the top keeps the tank wide open an' leaves left "
"an' right free to steer."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Reverse is half speed**, as it is from the keys, however far down the "
"cursor goes."
msgstr ""
"**Reverse is half speed**, same as from the keys, no matter how far down the "
"cursor goes."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**The box sets the speed asked for, not the speed you get at once.** A world "
"with an acceleration limit (BZFlag's `-a`, off by default) brings the tank "
"up to it over time, the same as it does from the keys."
msgstr ""
"**The box sets the speed ya ask fer, not the speed ya git right off.** A "
"world with an acceleration limit (BZFlag's `-a`, off unless somebody sets "
"it) brings the tank up to it over time, same as it does from the keys."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"The boxes are BZFlag's own sizes, scaled to the window. BZFlag also holds "
"the cursor inside the box; a browser cannot without taking the pointer over, "
"so in bzo the cursor can leave it -- the steering simply stays at full, and "
"the cost is a longer move back to the centre."
msgstr ""
"The boxes are BZFlag's own sizes, stretched to the window. BZFlag also keeps "
"the cursor penned inside the box; a browser can't without takin' the pointer "
"over, so in bzo the cursor can wander off -- the steerin' just stays at "
"full, an' it costs ya a longer haul back to the middle."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"With the keys, the mouse keeps whichever axis no key is holding -- see "
"[Combining inputs](#combining-inputs)."
msgstr ""
"With the keys, the mouse keeps whichever way no key's holdin' -- see [Mixin' "
"inputs](#combining-inputs)."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Clicks"
msgstr "Clickin'"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Left click shoots wherever the cursor is, whether mouse steering is on or "
"not, unless the click lands on the chat panel or a button. Right click "
"identifies. Mouse steering is unavailable with no mouse attached, in VR, and "
"while the on-screen controls are up, since those steer instead; a click that "
"misses one of their buttons does nothing rather than firing."
msgstr ""
"Left click shoots wherever the cursor's at, whether mouse steerin's on or "
"not, 'less the click lands on the chat panel or a button. Right click "
"figgers out who it is. Mouse steerin' ain't there with no mouse plugged in, "
"in VR, an' while the on-screen controls are up, since them steer instead; a "
"click that misses one of their buttons don't do nothin' 'stead of firin'."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Combining inputs"
msgstr "Mixin' inputs"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Every input drives at once, and nothing switches between them on its own: "
"`M` and the Settings rows are the only things that change which ones are on."
msgstr ""
"Ever' input drives all at once, an' nothin' switches between 'em on its own: "
"`M` an' the Settings rows are the only things that change which ones are on."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Driving is shared out an axis at a time** -- forward/back, and turn, each "
"on its own. On each, the first of these with something to say wins:"
msgstr ""
"**Drivin' gets shared out one way at a time** -- forward/back, an' turn, "
"each on its own. On each one, the first of these with somethin' to say wins:"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Keys.** A held drive key owns its axis, and holding both of a pair (`W` "
"and `S`, or `A` and `D`) is a deliberate stop on that axis."
msgstr ""
"**Keys.** A held drive key owns its way, an' holdin' both of a pair (`W` an' "
"`S`, or `A` an' `D`) is a stop on purpose that way."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**The stick:** the XR controllers in VR, otherwise a connected gamepad, "
"otherwise the on-screen stick. Only one of the three is read at a time -- "
"they are not added together."
msgstr ""
"**The stick:** the XR controllers in VR, otherwise a gamepad that's hooked "
"up, otherwise the on-screen stick. Only one of the three gets read at a time "
"-- they ain't added together."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "**The mouse**, in the targeting box, with mouse steering on."
msgstr "**The mouse**, in the aimin' box, with mouse steerin' on."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"So you can drive with `W` while the mouse steers, turn with `A`/`D` while "
"the mouse sets the speed, or steer a gamepad's turn while a key holds the "
"speed. A stick let go reads zero and gives the axis to the mouse; the mouse "
"box holds whatever the cursor's place says, which is why it comes last."
msgstr ""
"So ya can drive with `W` while the mouse steers, turn with `A`/`D` while the "
"mouse sets the speed, or steer a gamepad's turn while a key holds the speed. "
"A stick ya let go of reads zero an' hands that way to the mouse; the mouse "
"box holds whatever the cursor's spot says, which is why it comes last."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Buttons add up.** Shoot fires from `Enter`, a left click, or the stick "
"source's own fire button; jump from `Tab` or the stick source's; identify "
"from `I`, a right click, or the stick source's. Any of them will do."
msgstr ""
"**Buttons add up.** Shoot fires from `Enter`, a left click, or the stick's "
"own fire button; jump from `Tab` or the stick's; figger-out-who from `I`, a "
"right click, or the stick's. Any of 'em'll do."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**With the autopilot on**, the pilot takes the mouse's place, last in line: "
"a drive key or the stick you hold still owns its axis, and the pilot has the "
"rest. So when it is wedged against something you can hold `A` to turn it "
"out, or `S` to back it off, while it keeps the other axis, and let go to "
"hand it back -- it carries on from wherever you left it, re-planning its "
"route if you took it somewhere else. Your shots, jumps and drops add to its "
"own. The mouse box does not steer while the autopilot drives: it holds an "
"offset wherever the cursor is parked, so it would never hand anything back."
msgstr ""
"**With the autopilot on**, the pilot takes the mouse's place, last in line: "
"a drive key or the stick ya hold still owns its way, an' the pilot gits the "
"rest. So when it's wedged up against somethin' ya can hold `A` to turn it "
"out, or `S` to back it off, while it keeps the other way, an' let go to hand "
"it back -- it carries on from wherever ya left it, figgerin' a new route if "
"ya took it somewheres else. Yer shots, jumps an' drops add to its own. The "
"mouse box don't steer while the autopilot drives: it holds an offset "
"wherever the cursor's parked, so it wouldn't never hand nothin' back."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Menus don't stop the autopilot.** Opening Settings, or any other menu, "
"normally pauses your tank. With the autopilot driving, the menu takes the "
"keys and the pilot goes on driving. With a pilot chosen on the `Settings -> "
"Autopilot` row but not driving, opening a menu turns the autopilot on, and "
"closing the menu turns it off again -- so a menu means \"drive for me a "
"moment\" rather than \"stop\". With the row on `None`, the default, or on a "
"server that refuses bots (`-disableBots`), menus pause as they always have. "
"A hidden window still pauses either way: the browser stops drawing it, and "
"the pilot with it."
msgstr ""
"**Menus don't stop the autopilot.** Openin' Settings, or any other menu, "
"normally pauses yer tank. With the autopilot drivin', the menu takes the "
"keys an' the pilot keeps on drivin'. With a pilot picked on the `Settings -> "
"Autopilot` row but not drivin', openin' a menu turns the autopilot on, an' "
"shuttin' the menu turns it off again -- so a menu means \"drive fer me a "
"spell\" 'stead of \"stop\". With the row on `None`, the regular, or on a "
"server that won't have no bots (`-disableBots`), menus pause like they "
"always done. A hid window still pauses either way: the browser quits drawin' "
"it, an' the pilot with it."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**Three keys at once.** Many keyboards cannot report some three-key "
"combinations at all -- the third key's press never reaches the browser -- so "
"a held turn and reverse can swallow a jump (#146). The debug HUD (`` ` ``) "
"shows how many keys the browser saw held at once, which tells the keyboard's "
"limit from bzo's."
msgstr ""
"**Three keys at once.** Lotsa keyboards can't report some three-key combos "
"at all -- the third key's press never gits to the browser -- so a held turn "
"an' reverse can swaller a jump (#146). The debug HUD (`` ` ``) shows how "
"many keys the browser seen held at once, which tells the keyboard's limit "
"from bzo's."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Touch: the on-screen controls"
msgstr "Touch: the on-screen controls"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"A phone starts with them on; anywhere else `Settings -> Virtual Controls` "
"turns them on and off."
msgstr ""
"A phone starts with 'em on; anywheres else `Settings -> Virtual Controls` "
"turns 'em on an' off."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**The stick**, bottom left: push it to drive and turn, as far as you push "
"it. A mouse can drag it too."
msgstr ""
"**The stick**, bottom left: push it to drive an' turn, as far as ya push it. "
"A mouse can drag it too."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"**`●`** — shoot. Tapping fires as fast as clicking a mouse; holding fires at "
"the world's sustained rate"
msgstr ""
"**`●`** — shoot. Tappin' fires fast as clickin' a mouse; holdin' fires at "
"the world's steady rate"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "**`⤒`** — jump"
msgstr "**`⤒`** — jump"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "**`⚑`** — drop flag"
msgstr "**`⚑`** — drop the flag"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "**`◎`** — identify, and lock a Guided Missile"
msgstr "**`◎`** — figger out who it is, an' lock a Guided Missile"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Everything else -- camera, radar range, chat, hunting, autopilot, pausing -- "
"is a row in Settings, which a tap reaches."
msgstr ""
"Ever'thing else -- camera, radar range, chat, huntin', autopilot, pausin' -- "
"is a row in Settings, which a tap gits to."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Gamepad"
msgstr "Gamepad"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Any controller the browser reports in the standard layout (most USB and "
"Bluetooth pads, and iOS MFi controllers). Plugging one in turns it on; "
"nothing needs setting up."
msgstr ""
"Any controller the browser reports in the standard layout (most USB an' "
"Bluetooth pads, an' iOS MFi controllers). Pluggin' one in turns it on; there "
"ain't nothin' to set up."

#: docs/help/controls.md
