msgstr "`X` / Square"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "drop flag"
msgstr "drop the flag"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Either shoulder"
msgstr "Either shoulder"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "identify"
msgstr "figger out who"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"The sticks have a dead zone of a fifth of their travel, so a pad left on the "
"desk does not creep. The right stick is free."
msgstr ""
"The sticks got a dead zone of a fifth of their travel, so a pad left settin' "
"on the desk don't creep. The right stick's free."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"The pad rumbles when you fire and when your tank dies, as BZFlag's does: a "
"short buzz for a shot, longer for a shock wave, both motors for a laser, and "
"one long, strong shake for a death. It rumbles only while it is what you are "
"playing with -- a key or a click hands control back and keeps it quiet -- "
"and never for an observer. **Rumble** in Settings turns it off. The browser "
"has to support it; Chrome and Edge do."
msgstr ""
"The pad rumbles when ya fire an' when yer tank dies, same as BZFlag's: a "
"short buzz fer a shot, longer fer a shock wave, both motors fer a laser, an' "
"one long, hard shake fer a death. It only rumbles while it's what yer "
"playin' with -- a key or a click hands control back an' keeps it hushed -- "
"an' never fer an observer. **Rumble** in Settings turns it off. The "
"browser's gotta support it; Chrome an' Edge do."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "XR controllers"
msgstr "XR controllers"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"In VR the controllers are the only input. Turning the tank is independent of "
"where you look."
msgstr ""
"In VR the controllers are the only input. Turnin' the tank don't care where "
"yer lookin'."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "In the XR menu"
msgstr "In the XR menu"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Either thumbstick"
msgstr "Either thumbstick"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "forward/backward and turn -- the right stick if both are pushed"
msgstr "forward/back an' turn -- the right stick if both are pushed"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Either trigger"
msgstr "Either trigger"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`A` / `X` (primary face button)"
msgstr "`A` / `X` (main face button)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "`B` / `Y` (secondary face button)"
msgstr "`B` / `Y` (other face button)"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "open the XR menu"
msgstr "open the XR menu"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "back, and close it from the top"
msgstr "back, an' shut it from the top"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Either grip"
msgstr "Either grip"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Press either thumbstick"
msgstr "Press either thumbstick"

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid "Both controllers pulse for the same events as a gamepad's rumble."
msgstr "Both controllers thump fer the same doin's as a gamepad's rumble."

#: docs/help/controls.md
msgid ""
"Identify is on the thumbstick press because a thumb that is steering presses "
"it by accident, and identifying costs nothing; the menu is on `B` for the "
"same reason. Typing -- a name, a MOTD -- uses the headset's own system "
"keyboard, raised when the row takes focus; see the README's WebXR section "
"for headsets that have none."
msgstr ""
"Figger-out-who is on the thumbstick press 'cause a thumb that's steerin' "
"presses it by accident, an' figgerin' out who costs nothin'; the menu's on "
"`B` fer the same reason. Typin' -- a name, a MOTD -- uses the headset's own "
"system keyboard, brung up when the row takes focus; see the README's WebXR "
"section fer headsets that ain't got one."

#: docs/help/flags.md
msgid "Flags"
msgstr "Flags"

#: docs/help/flags.md
msgid ""
"Drive over a flag to pick it up, and `Space` to drop it. Good flags help; "
"bad flags hinder, and stay until they shake off, you kill, or you die. A "
"superflag on the ground is white and tells you nothing about itself until "
"somebody picks it up. Team flags are captured by carrying an enemy's to your "
"own base."
msgstr ""
"Drive over a flag to pick it up, an' `Space` to drop it. Good flags help; "
"bad flags hold ya back, an' they stick around till they shake off, ya kill "
"somebody, or ya die. A superflag on the ground is white an' don't tell ya "
"nothin' about itself till somebody picks it up. Team flags git captured by "
"haulin' an enemy's back to yer own base."

#: docs/help/scoreboard.md
msgid "Scoreboard"
msgstr "Scoreboard"

#: docs/help/scoreboard.md
msgid ""
"Each row's numbers read **Kills / Deaths**, then **[Team Kills]** once you "
"have any, then your own record against that one opponent: **wins~losses**, "
"blank until you've actually fought them. Your own row shows a self-destruct "
"count there instead, since you have no record against yourself. Rabbit Chase "
"adds a rank percentage in front of the kill count."
msgstr ""
"Each row's numbers read **Kills / Deaths**, then **[Team Kills]** once ya "
"got any, then yer own record against that one feller: **wins~losses**, blank "
"till y'all actually tangled. Yer own row shows a blowed-yerself-up count "
"there instead, since ya ain't got no record against yerself. Rabbit Chase "
"sticks a rank percentage out front of the kill count."

#: docs/help/scoreboard.md
msgid ""
"Before a name, in cyan: `@` means that player is an admin, `+` means they're "
"signed in with a verified callsign this session. Neither shows for anyone "
"else."
msgstr ""
"Before a name, in cyan: `@` means that player's an admin, `+` means they're "
"signed in with a verified callsign this session. Neither one shows fer "
"nobody else."

#: docs/help/scoreboard.md
msgid ""
"Right after the name itself: a `/XX` is the flag they're carrying, in that "
"flag's own colour -- see [Flags](flags.md) for what each abbreviation means."
msgstr ""
"Right after the name itself: a `/XX` is the flag they're totin', in that "
"flag's own colour -- see [Flags](flags.md) fer what each abbreviation means."

#: docs/help/scoreboard.md
msgid ""
"Further along the name: 🎤 means that player's microphone is on, and 🔊 "
"replaces it the moment they're actually speaking. ⏳ means paused. A hunted "
"player wears a cyan `◎` -- see [Hunting](controls.md#hunting)."
msgstr ""
"Further along the name: 🎤 means that player's microphone is on, an' 🔊 takes "
"its place the second they're actually jawin'. ⏳ means paused. A hunted "
"player wears a cyan `◎` -- see [Huntin'](controls.md#hunting)."

#: docs/help/voice.md
msgid "Audio and voice"
msgstr "Sound an' jawin'"

#: docs/help/voice.md
msgid ""
"`Settings -> Audio Settings` — game, voice, and microphone levels, each from "
"Off to 100%"
msgstr ""
"`Settings -> Audio Settings` — game, voice, an' microphone levels, each from "
"Off to 100%"

#: docs/help/voice.md
msgid ""
"**Voice channel** — **All** is everyone on the server, **Nearby** is only "
"players within earshot, **Team** is your own team anywhere on the map"
msgstr ""
"**Voice channel** — **All** is ever'body on the server, **Nearby** is only "
"players within hollerin' distance, **Team** is yer own team anywheres on the "
"map"

#: docs/help/voice.md
msgid "`B` — toggle the microphone"
msgstr "`B` — flip the microphone"

#: docs/help/voice.md
msgid ""
"Voice is available after microphone permission is granted. Observers talk "
"and listen on the same terms as everyone else."
msgstr ""
"Voice works once ya let it have the microphone. Observers talk an' listen "
"same as ever'body else."

